# Demo interaction asset contract

The four storylines may be redesigned independently. Treat reusable interaction
capabilities as a shared asset layer, not as story-specific implementations.

Source of truth: `superagent/INTERACTION-ASSET-INVENTORY.md`.

When implementing a change in `superagent/**` or `workbench/**`:

- If the user calls it an asset-level change, update the inventory in the same task.
- Also update it proactively when a new or changed interaction can serve two or more storylines.
- Record interaction structure, visual pattern, state, feedback, trigger, dismissal,
  reuse scope, maturity, and primary implementation files.
- Do not add story-specific roles, dialogue, fixed mock data, or one-off plot order
  to the asset inventory; keep those in the relevant storyline document.
- Mark assets as reusable, composable, demo-only, hidden, placeholder, or needing consolidation.
- When replacing, hiding, or retiring an asset, preserve the entry and update its status
  and replacement instead of silently deleting it.
- Separate story orchestration changes from shared asset changes when both occur together.
- Reuse an existing asset before creating another interaction pattern with the same semantics.

Do not infer or lock the names or content of the four new storylines from the old UJ-1 / UJ-2 / UJ-3 documents.
